 "timezone_determination": {
  "zeqdb": "UTC (GMT). Evidence: 2025-04-23 M6.2 Marmara listed 09:49:09 (known UTC 09:49); 2019-09-26 Silivri listed 10:59:24 (known UTC 10:59); 2014-05-24 Gokceada M6.8 listed 09:25:01 (known UTC 09:25; local summer time would be 12:25 -> proves UTC also pre-2016, no DST handling needed). Times used as-is.",
  "monthly_xml": "Turkey local time UTC+3. Evidence: 2025-10-02 anchor (11:55 UTC) appears as 2025.10.02 14:55:03 in monthly_202510.xml; hgmmap.asp UI labels lists 'Yerel saat'; empirical cross-match of 352 March-2026 events monthly-vs-zeqdb gives median |residual| 0.0 s after converting local->UTC via zoneinfo Europe/Istanbul. Converted to UTC.",
  "live_lst0.asp": "Turkey local time (newest event 15:05 local while fetch time was ~12:56 UTC). Not used in catalog (last-500 only); saved as probe.",
  "afad_api": "UTC. Evidence: same 2025-10-02 anchor returned as 2025-10-02T11:55:03.",
  "pre2016_dst_note": "Turkiye observed summer DST (civil UTC+2 winter / UTC+3 summer) until Sept 2016, then permanent UTC+3. A civil-local mis-read would shift pre-2016 events +2h (winter) / +3h (summer). REJECTED empirically in BOTH seasons: cross-match of 21 well-recorded pre-2016 box events against USGS/NEIC authoritative UTC (scripts/verify/tz_anchors.py -> results/tz_anchor_crosscheck.json) gives max|residual| 2.0s over 4 winter anchors (2013-01-08 M5.7, 2010-11-03 M5.3, 2009-02-17 M5.2, 2008-12-28 M5.2) and 2.7s over 17 summer anchors; the +2h/+3h signatures are absent, so zeqdb is true UTC year-round and no offset is applied. Monthly XMLs (2026 tail only, features-only) are civil time converted DST-aware via zoneinfo('Europe/Istanbul')."
 },
